## 📝 Structure for **Archive** subpage (feature summary)

Use the **Archive** subpage under Task (`archivePageUrl`, title e.g. `Archive <taskId>`). Notion already shows the page title—start the body at `##` per **`Core/memory-bank-paths.mdc`**.

  * **Feature Title:** (e.g., "User Profile — Avatar Upload Enhancement")
  * **Feature ID:** from Task row **Task ID** / config `taskId`
  * **Date Archived:** YYYY-MM-DD
  * **Status:** COMPLETED & ARCHIVED
  * **1. Feature Overview:**
      * Brief description of the feature and its purpose (from **Task page body** or **Project page body**).
      * Link to the Task page or plan section (`<mention-page>`).
  * **2. Key Requirements Met:**
      * Main functional and non-functional requirements addressed.
  * **3. Design Decisions & Creative Outputs:**
      * Summary of key design choices.
      * Links to all relevant **Creative** subpages.
      * Link to **style-guide** subpage (`styleGuidePageUrl`) if applicable.
  * **4. Implementation Summary:**
      * High-level overview of implementation.
      * Primary new components/modules.
      * Key technologies or libraries.
      * Link to merge commit, PR, or primary code location.
  * **5. Testing Overview:**
      * Testing strategy (unit, integration, E2E) and outcomes.
  * **6. Reflection & Lessons Learned:**
      * Link to **Reflection** subpage (`reflectionPageUrl`).
      * Optionally, copy 1–2 critical lessons into the archive summary.
  * **7. Known Issues or Future Considerations (Optional):**
      * Deferred minor issues.
      * Future enhancements.

### Key files and components affected (from Task page body)

[Summary or checklist from the **Task page body** for this feature—scope of repo files and components touched.]

## 📌 What to Emphasize in L3 Archiving

  * **Self-contained feature record:** One **Archive** subpage (plus links) tells the story of the feature.
  * **Traceability:** Easy navigation to Task body, Creative, Reflection, and Progress.
  * **Maintainability:** What a future developer needs to extend or fix this feature.
  * **Not a full system archive:** Unlike Level 4, this closes one significant feature, not the whole application state.
